  "drivers": [],
  "summary": "Katie Ledecky is currently the most decorated female U.S. Olympian in history, possessing 14 total medals (9 gold) and 23 World Championship titles. Despite transitioning into a mature stage of her athletic career—marked by a historic gold-medal sweep at Paris 2024 and her first career defeats in her signature distance events at the August 2026 Pan Pacific Championships—she remains an elite global authority in competitive swimming. Off the pool deck, her audience is solid, commanding approximately 1.4 million followers across Instagram, Facebook, and X. Though she lacks a native presence on TikTok, her cultural relevance is highly elevated. She is a recipient of the Presidential Medal of Freedom (2024), a Yale honorary doctorate (2026), and has a New York Times best-selling memoir, Just Add Water, which revealed her battle with POTS. Financially, Ledecky is backed by blue-chip, multi-million dollar deals with TYR Sport, Athleta, and Visa. Her momentum is stable and mature, trending steadily as she targets her fifth Olympic games in Los Angeles 2028. The primary missing information is private social engagement performance (such as saves, shares, and video retention) and confidential brand campaign conversion data.",
